  "summary": "Neko Network's Aave-style MainPool 0x4071ee5eb20ba7352dcf08cabc7da4fa1daa370c implements borrow(asset, amount, onBehalfOf) by minting the variable-debt token to onBehalfOf and paying the borrowed underlying to msg.sender, with no borrow-allowance or delegation check. The debt token's mint(address,uint256) takes no caller argument. Any account could therefore borrow against another depositor's collateral and keep the funds. Six attacker accounts and two attacker contracts made 196 such borrows against 16 depositors, taking 3,620,179 USDT, 499,424.04 BUSD, 2,792.84 USDC and 1 BTCB.",
